commit 69538ae878406e5cb8ff3a42fda474271f56ed2b
Author: [REDACTED-USER] <[REDACTED-INTERNAL-EMAIL]>
Date:   Fri Aug 14 16:42:33 2026 +0800

    feat(bk7258): add read-only SD-NAND SDIO port

    Add the BK7258 SDIO PIO lower-half, SDIO PWC clock handshake, GPIO setup, MMCSD fixed-geometry read-only fallback, FAT/MBR configuration, and the periph_selftest block-driver checks.

    The implementation is intentionally limited to 1-bit polling reads and does not enable DMA, writes, formatting, or destructive tests. It follows the vendor BK7258 V2 register base, CMD18/CMD12 framing, FIFO reset, clock-gate, W1C, and CRC error handling as far as the current lower-half supports.

    Hardware verification completed: -Werror build, Armino packaging, autoflash, card identification through CMD8/ACMD41/CMD2/CMD3/CMD9/CMD7/CMD16/ACMD51, and all non-storage self-tests pass.

    Known limitation: sector data integrity is not yet valid on the target. The latest run reports DATA_CRC_FAIL (0x1004a4c0), sector 0 read -5, and SELFTEST FAIL failures=1. MBR/VFAT mount validation remains blocked. The next required step is to port the vendor ISR/semaphore receive path instead of accepting CRC-failed or misframed PIO data.

